-- title:
--   History $\sigma$-algebra before round $t$
-- statement:
--   For a run and a round $t$, the history before round $t$ is the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the draws $(I_s,S_s,U_s)$ and the responses $V_s$ of all rounds $s<t$.
--
--   The objective sequence is deterministic (it is fixed by an oblivious adversary), so it contributes nothing to this $\sigma$-algebra; the states $x_s$, $s\le t$, are functions of the history through the projection update.
-- source:
--   Aggarwal–Lu, Geometry-Dependent Online and Offline Approximation for Non-Monotone DR-Submodular Maximization, arXiv:2610.00545, Section 3.2, p.9 (after (6)); Lemma 5.2, p.19

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GeomDRSub_Alg1Run
import Definitions.Def_GeomDRSub_Alg1Run_draws

namespace GeomDRSub

/-- **The history before round `t`.** Aggarwal–Lu, arXiv:2610.00545, p.9 (after (6)) and
Lemma 5.2, p.19: the information of "all choices and responses preceding" round `t`.

`R.hist t` is the σ-algebra generated by the draws `(I_s, S_s, U_s)` and the responses `V_s` of all
rounds `s < t`.

**Formalization Note.** The objective sequence is deterministic (oblivious adversary), so it adds
nothing to the σ-algebra. The states `x_s`, `s ≤ t`, are functions of this history through the
projection update. -/
def Alg1Run.hist {d : ℕ} {Ω : Type*} (R : Alg1Run d Ω) (t : ℕ) : MeasurableSpace Ω :=
  ⨆ s, ⨆ (_ : s < t), MeasurableSpace.comap (fun ω => (R.draws s ω, R.V s ω)) inferInstance

end GeomDRSub


